{"unit":9,"section":1,"cefr":"Intro","objective":"describe animals","skill":"Animals","heading":"Describe animals","phrases":[{"he":"יש לי צב.","en":"I have a turtle.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/cf61df06b883f2b2aff5b645379521dc","tokens":[{"w":"יש","h":["I have","have","there are","has"]},{"w":"לי","h":["I have","me","to me","for me"]},{"w":"צב","h":["a turtle","turtle","a tortoise"]}]},{"he":"זה נשר?","en":"Is that an eagle?","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/50435529bc66afbb1794d8ea737c40af","tokens":[{"w":"זה","h":["this is","this","it is"]},{"w":"נשר","h":["an eagle","eagle","vulture"]}]},{"he":"החתול שותֶה את החלב.","en":"The cat drinks the milk.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/b0ae839115c5edc43df4092324a0d601","tokens":[{"w":"החתול","h":["the cat"]},{"w":"שותֶה","h":["drinks","drink","is drinking"]},{"w":"את","h":["the milk","you"]},{"w":"החלב","h":["the milk","the milk","milk","the milk is"]}]},{"he":"לא, הכלב לא נובח.","en":"No, the dog is not barking.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/3fdadfc9bac392647d268d8dcd3f12f4","tokens":[{"w":"לא","h":["is not","not","no"]},{"w":"הכלב","h":["the dog"]},{"w":"לא","h":["is not","not","no"]},{"w":"נובח","h":["is barking","barking","bark"]}]}],"words":[{"he":"שותֶה","en":"drinks","alt":["drink","drinking","is drinking"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"החלב","en":"the milk","alt":["milk","the milk is"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"הכלב","en":"the dog","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"צב","en":"a turtle","alt":["a tortoise","turtle"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"נשר","en":"an eagle","alt":["eagle","vulture"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"החתול","en":"the cat","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"נובח","en":"barking","alt":["bark","is barking"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"יש","en":"I have","alt":["have","there are","has"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"לי","en":"I have","alt":["me","to me","for me"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"זה","en":"this","alt":["this is","it is"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"את","en":"the milk","alt":["you"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"לא","en":"is not","alt":["not","no"],"from":"phrase"}],"lexemes":["זנב","סרטן","קופה","הפרה","פיל","הפילה","חמור","עכביש","הפיל","החמור","הקוף","העכביש","קוף","פרה","הנשר","נשר","זבוב","חיית מחמד"],"tips":"In Hebrew some animals have both masculine and feminine forms. If we use the masculine form, we are referring to a male animal, and if we use the feminine form, we are referring to a female animal.\n\nIn order to turn the masculine form of an animal into its feminine form, we often simply add \"ה\" to the end of the noun.\n\nFor example:\n\n>A male cat - חתול (khatúl)\n\n>A female cat - חתול**ה** (khatul**á**)\n\nSome animals receive the letter \"ת\" instead of \"ה\".\n\nFor example:\n\n>A male rabbit - ארנב (arnáv)\n\n>A female rabbit - ארנב**ת** (arnév**et**) (The vowels also change a bit here. You will get used to seeing this pattern as you learn new words.)\n\nNote that ציפור (bird) is **feminine**, even though it ends in ים in the plural. It is irregular:\n\nציפורים שרות - Birds are singing. tsiporím sharót"}